<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Shutdown (255)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>shutdown
</pre>
<p>Stops the game at once, without a countdown: every player is told 
"Shutdown by &lt;your name&gt;.", is saved, and the server exits. Type the 
command in full; an abbreviation is refused.
</p><p>Note that the script that keeps the game running (runvme.sh) starts the 
server again whenever it exits, so on a server run that way, shutdown 
works like an unannounced reboot. To keep the game down, stop the 
scripts on the server (bin/stopvme.sh). To restart with a warning to the 
players, use <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Reboot</a>.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Reboot</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Crash</a>
</pre>




</div>